Z||000000||gargoyle||08-27-2001||06:59 PM||||Last night went I went to back out of my driveway, I couldn't. I can't select reverse and I found out later, 5th. I checked my manual and there is an alignment for the cable. Is this my possible problem. No matter how far over I push the shifter, they can't be selected. Also has anybody done this alignment. This is on a 87 GT. Is this a better 2 person thing. Quoting I believe Vincent Price from The Fly "help me, help me"    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>[This message has been edited by gargoyle (edited 08-27-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by gargoyle (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||Wolfhound||08-27-2001||07:30 PM||||Broken selector cable!<BR>When the cable breaks 3rd and 4th are neutral for the selector. The broken cable will still push to give 1st and 2nd but will not pull to give you 5th and reverse.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gargoyle||08-27-2001||07:43 PM||||In reference to above reply. @#$%^!##$*****!!!!<BR>Oh the joy of owning a new used car.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000003||Wolfhound||08-27-2001||08:38 PM||||In reference to your post in the mall. there are two cables, one controls the front to rear movement and is called the shift cable. The other cable is called the selector cableand controls the gate. <P>Yeah, mine broke about 15 minutes after I was asked if I had every had a problem with reverse,??? Go figure!  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||08-27-2001||09:06 PM||||86/87 shift cables for 5 speed<P>Select cable part # 10054258 (usually the one that goes)<BR>Shift Cable part # 10066448<BR> <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com</A>  I think I paid $153 for one and $168 for the other + shipping.  I don't remember which was which.<P>||||reg||1
